   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "El passato prossimo",
    "@en": "The prossimo passage"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Para contar algo terminado se usa con mucha frecuencia el **passato prossimo**. Con muchos verbos se forma con el presente de **avere** + el **participio**: **Ho mangiato** (comí / he comido). La traducción natural depende del contexto.",
     "@en": "The **passato prossimo** is often used to count something finished. With many verbs it is formed with the present of **avere** + the **participio**: **Ho mangiato** (ate / have eaten). Natural translation depends on the context."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Pauta regular para el participio: **-are → -ato** (mangiare → mangiato), **-ere → -uto** (vendere → venduto), **-ire → -ito** (dormire → dormito). Hay muchos participios frecuentes irregulares, que se aprenden caso por caso.",
     "@en": "Regular practice for the participle: **-are → -ato** (mangiare → mangiato), **-ere → -uto** (sell → bandage), **-ire → -ito** (sleep → sleeping). There are many frequent irregular participles, which are learned on a case-by-case basis."
    }
   ]
